PR #92's CI failed on:
  ERROR: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md is out of date: generated 17 commits ago,
  exceeds the 15-commit window

Not a defect in the change under review. The five verify-generated --check
gates were pre-flighted green BEFORE pushing, but auto-pr then rebased this
branch onto a dev that had advanced (tracker sync + the WI-gapir merge), and
the check keys on commit-count DISTANCE — so the window moved underneath the
pre-flight and the recorded commit fell outside it.

Worth recording because the standing mitigation ('pre-flight the
verify-generated gates before every auto-pr') is necessary but NOT sufficient:
it is invalidated by auto-pr's own rebase whenever dev moves between the
pre-flight and the push, which a tracker auto-sync makes routine. The reliable
form is to re-check AFTER the rebase, or to regenerate as part of recovery.

